{The parent uses a fixed equal-weight H0/H1 blend. The single modification hypothesis is to increase H0's weight smoothly with relative dispersion in unfinished-job remaining work, since H0 rewards larger remaining work whereas H1 penalizes estimated tail work. Equal weights remain when remaining work is uniform; the adjustment is bounded and does not presume demonstrated improvement.}
```python
def use_heuristics(progress, candidate_pair_ratio, remaining_work_mean, remaining_work_std, machine_ready_mean, machine_ready_std, previous_heuristic):
    dispersion = remaining_work_std / (remaining_work_mean + remaining_work_std)
    alpha = 0.5 + 0.25 * dispersion
    return (1, (alpha, 1.0 - alpha, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0))
```
